/-!
# The numerical type of the special fibre of a regular model

Let `R` be a local ring of Krull dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, with residue field `k`, and let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme,
proper and flat over `Spec R`, all of whose points have codimension at most two, whose generic
point lies outside the special fibre, and whose special fibre is connected. Assuming that `H⁰` and
`H¹` of the structure sheaf of every irreducible component `Cᵢ` of the special fibre (with its
reduced induced structure) are finite-dimensional over `k`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology`), this file packages the
component set, multiplicities `mᵢ`, constant-field weights `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k]`, intersection matrix
`aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)` and constant-field genera `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` into a
`TauCeti.NumericalType`, following
[Stacks, Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U).

The five axioms of an abstract numerical type come from the special-fibre intersection and weight
theories:

* nonemptiness of the component set is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.nonempty_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint`, using properness of
  `X → Spec R`;
* symmetry, off-diagonal nonnegativity, connectedness of the positive-entry graph and the fibre
  relation `∑ⱼ mⱼ aᵢⱼ = 0` are proved in `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Matrix`;
* divisibility `wᵢ ∣ aᵢⱼ` of the `i`-th row by the weight of `Cᵢ` is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`.

Because any two nonzerodivisor generators of the maximal ideal of `R` are unit multiples of each
other (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_of_span_eq`), the packaged
numerical type does not depend on the choice of generator `π`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_congr`). For a proper regular integral
`TauCeti.Model` of relative dimension at most one over a discrete valuation ring, this gives a
uniformizer-free invariant `TauCeti.Model.numericalType` in which Noetherianity of the total space,
the codimension-two bound and generic-point separation from the closed point are discharged
automatically.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`: the numerical type of the connected
  special fibre of a proper flat regular integral scheme of dimension at most two over `R`.
* `TauCeti.Model.numericalType`: the uniformizer-free numerical type of a proper regular integral
  model of relative dimension at most one over a discrete valuation ring.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_congr`: the packaged numerical type is
  strictly independent of the chosen nonzerodivisor generator of the maximal ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff`: two components are adjacent in
  the numerical type if and only if they are distinct and meet in `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.forall_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff`: every
  component has multiplicity one if and only if the scheme-theoretic special fibre is reduced.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow`:
  each term `wᵢ (gᵢ - 1)` is `-χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, expressing the signed genus of the numerical type in
  terms of the truncated Euler characteristics of the reduced components and their
  self-intersections.
* `TauCeti.Model.numericalType_eq_specialFiberNumericalType`: for any uniformizer of the discrete
  valuation ring, `M.numericalType` is equal to `M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z) and
  [Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U).
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open scoped Matrix
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

section SpecialFiberNumericalType

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.DimensionLEOne R]
  {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R))
  [Flat toBase] [IsProper toBase] [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X]

/-- **The numerical type of the special fibre of a regular model.** Let `X` be a regular Noetherian
integral scheme, proper and flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal
is generated by a nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two, generic point
outside the special fibre, and connected special fibre. When `H⁰` and `H¹` of the structure sheaf
of every reduced irreducible component of the special fibre are finite-dimensional over the residue
field of `R`, the components, their multiplicities, their constant-field weights, their
intersection matrix and their constant-field genera form a `TauCeti.NumericalType`
([Stacks, Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U)). -/
@[expose]
def specialFiberNumericalType
    (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
    {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
    (h₀ : toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
    (h₁ : toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R})) :
    NumericalType.{u} where
  Component := (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
    (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset
  componentFintype := inferInstance
  componentDecidableEq := Classical.decEq _
  componentNonempty :=
    let ⟨c, hc⟩ := toBase.nonempty_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint hη
    ⟨⟨c, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hc⟩⟩
  multiplicity i :=
    ⟨toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i,
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_pos hη (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π)
        (toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ) i
        ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2)⟩
  weight i :=
    ⟨toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2),
      toBase.specialFiberWeight_pos ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2)
        (h₀ i ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))⟩
  intersection := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  intersection_isSymm := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη h₀ h₁
  offDiagonal_nonneg _ _ hij :=
    toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_nonneg_of_ne hX hη h₀ h₁ hij
  connected := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_reflTransGen hX hη h₀ h₁ hconn
  fiber_relation i := by
    have h := congrFun
      (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_mulVec_specialFiberMultiplicity
        hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg) i
    rw [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Pi.zero_apply] at h
    exact (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ ↦ mul_comm _ _).trans h
  weight_dvd := toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  genus i :=
    Module.finrank
      Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
      (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)

section API

variable (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2)
  (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
  (h₀ : toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
  (h₁ : toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
  (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))

/-- The component index type of `specialFiberNumericalType` is the finite set of codimension-one
points of `X` lying over the closed point. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_component :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component =
      (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset :=
  (rfl)

/-- A codimension-one point of `X` arises as a component of `specialFiberNumericalType` if and only
if it maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem exists_specialFiberNumericalType_component_iff (x : CodimensionOnePoint X) :
    (∃ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component, i.1 = x) ↔
      toBase x = closedPoint R :=
  ⟨by
    rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2,
    fun hx ↦ ⟨⟨x, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hx⟩, rfl⟩⟩

/-- Every component of `specialFiberNumericalType` maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem base_specialFiberNumericalType_component
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    toBase i.1 = closedPoint R :=
  (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2

/-- The multiplicity of a component in `specialFiberNumericalType` is its special-fibre
multiplicity `ord_{Cᵢ}(π)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.1 :=
  (rfl)

/-- The weight of a component in `specialFiberNumericalType` is the residue-field dimension
`dim_k H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` of its constant field. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_specialFiberNumericalType_weight
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberWeight
        (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The intersection matrix of `specialFiberNumericalType` is the special-fibre intersection
matrix `(Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_intersection
    (i j : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).intersection i j =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j :=
  (rfl)

/-- The genus of a component in `specialFiberNumericalType` is `dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` over its
own constant field `κᵢ = Γ(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_genus
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank
        Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
        (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Two components are adjacent in `specialFiberNumericalType` if and only if they are distinct
and their closures in `X` meet. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff
    (i j : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Adj i j ↔
      i ≠ j ∧ (closure {(i.1 : X)} ∩ closure {(j.1 : X)}).Nonempty := by
  rw [NumericalType.adj_iff, specialFiberNumericalType_intersection]
  exact and_congr_right fun hij ↦
    toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_pos_iff hX hη h₀ h₁ hij

/-- **Generator independence of the special-fibre numerical type.** Any two nonzerodivisor
generators of the maximal ideal of `R` define the exact same `NumericalType`: the component set,
weights, intersection matrix and genera do not mention the generator, and the multiplicities agree
by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_of_span_eq`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_congr {π' : R}
    (hπ' : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π'}) (hreg' : IsSMulRegular R π') :
    toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn =
      toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ' hreg' h₀ h₁ hconn := by
  suffices ∀ (m m' : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
        (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset → ℕ+)
      (hf : ∀ i, ∑ j, (m j : ℤ) * toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j = 0)
      (hf' : ∀ i, ∑ j, (m' j : ℤ) * toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i j = 0),
      m = m' →
      ({ toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn with
          multiplicity := m, fiber_relation := hf } : NumericalType) =
      { toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn with
          multiplicity := m', fiber_relation := hf' } by
    refine this _ _ _ _ (funext fun i ↦ Subtype.ext ?_)
    exact toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_of_span_eq (hπ.symm.trans hπ') hreg i.1
  rintro m _ _ _ rfl
  rfl

/-- Every component of `specialFiberNumericalType` has multiplicity one if and only if the
scheme-theoretic special fibre is reduced. -/
theorem forall_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff :
    (∀ i, (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i = 1) ↔
      IsReduced (specialFiber R toBase).left := by
  rw [toBase.isReduced_specialFiber_iff_specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_one_of_isRegular hX hη hπ]
  refine ⟨fun h x hx ↦ ?_, fun h i ↦ ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, rfl⟩ :=
      (toBase.exists_specialFiberNumericalType_component_iff hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn x).mpr hx
    exact PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mpr (h i)
  · exact PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mp
      (h i.1 (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i))

/-- For each component `Cᵢ` of the special fibre, `wᵢ gᵢ = dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i))
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℕ) *
        (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) := by
  rw [coe_specialFiberNumericalType_weight, specialFiberNumericalType_genus]
  exact toBase.specialFiberWeight_mul_finrank_cohomology_one
    (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i)

/-- For each component `Cᵢ` of the special fibre, `wᵢ (gᵢ - 1) = -χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, where `χ_k` is the
degree-`2` truncated Euler characteristic `dim_k H⁰ - dim_k H¹` over the residue field. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one
    (i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
        (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i))
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
        (((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i : ℤ) - 1) =
      -Scheme.Modules.eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
        (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2 := by
  have hi := toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i
  let := subschemeOverResidueField
    (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hi)
  have hwg :
      ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i : ℤ) =
        (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) : ℤ) := by
    exact_mod_cast
      toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i
  have hw0 :
      ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℤ) =
        (Module.finrank (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0) : ℤ) := by
    rw [coe_specialFiberNumericalType_weight, specialFiberWeight_def]
  rw [Scheme.Modules.eulerCharBelow_two, mul_sub, mul_one, hwg, hw0]
  ring

/-- Weighted sum of `mᵢ wᵢ (gᵢ - 1)` across the components of `specialFiberNumericalType`, equal to
`-∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
theorem sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one :
    ∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
        ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℤ) *
          (((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i : ℤ) - 1) =
      -∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
        ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
          (letI := subschemeOverResidueField
            (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
              (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i))
          Scheme.Modules.eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
            (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
            (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2) := by
  rw [← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ ↦ ?_
  rw [mul_assoc,
    toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_weight_mul_genus_sub_one hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i,
    mul_neg]

/-- The signed genus of `specialFiberNumericalType` expressed directly in terms of the truncated
Euler characteristics `χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ})` of the reduced components and their self-intersections:
`g(T) = 1 - ∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ}) - (∑ᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cᵢ)) / 2`. -/
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).arithmeticGenus =
      1 - (∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (letI := subschemeOverResidueField
              (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
                (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i))
            Scheme.Modules.eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
              (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
                (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2)) -
        (∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i i) / 2 := by
  rw [NumericalType.arithmeticGenus_def,
    toBase.sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one
      hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn]
  simp only [specialFiberNumericalType_intersection]
  ring

/-- Division-free form of `specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow`:
`2 g(T) = 2 - 2 ∑ᵢ mᵢ χ_k(𝒪_{Cᵢ}) - ∑ᵢ mᵢ (Cᵢ · Cᵢ)`. -/
theorem two_mul_specialFiberNumericalType_arithmeticGenus_eq_sum_eulerCharBelow :
    2 * (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).arithmeticGenus =
      2 - 2 * (∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            (letI := subschemeOverResidueField
              (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton
                (toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn i))
            Scheme.Modules.eulerCharBelow (ResidueField R)
              (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme
              (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
                (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 2)) -
        ∑ i : (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).Component,
          ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℤ) *
            toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη i i := by
  rw [NumericalType.two_mul_arithmeticGenus,
    toBase.sum_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_mul_weight_mul_genus_sub_one
      hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn]
  simp only [specialFiberNumericalType_intersection]
  ring

end API

end SpecialFiberNumericalType

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace TauCeti.Model

variable {R K : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
  [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
  {C : Scheme.{u}} {toK : C ⟶ Spec (.of K)}

/-- **The numerical type of a proper regular model.** For a proper integral regular model `M` of
relative dimension at most one over a discrete valuation ring `R`, with connected special fibre and
finite-dimensional `H⁰` and `H¹` on the reduced irreducible components of the special fibre, this
is the uniformizer-independent `TauCeti.NumericalType` of the special fibre. Both `[M.IsProper]`
and `[RelativeDimensionLE 1 M.toBase]` are synthesized automatically whenever
`[FamilyOfCurves M.toBase]` is in scope. -/
@[expose]
def numericalType (M : Model R K C toK) [M.IsProper]
    [RelativeDimensionLE 1 M.toBase] [IsIntegral M.total]
    [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular M.total]
    (h₀ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
    (h₁ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
    (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (M.toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R})) :
    NumericalType.{u} :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType
    M.toBase.coheight_le_succ_of_relativeDimensionLE
    (M.toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field R))
    (IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.maximalIdeal_eq
    (mul_right_injective₀ (IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.ne_zero)
    h₀ h₁ hconn

section ModelAPI

variable (M : Model R K C toK) [M.IsProper]
  [RelativeDimensionLE 1 M.toBase] [IsIntegral M.total]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular M.total]
  (h₀ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 0)
  (h₁ : M.toBase.FiniteDimensionalComponentCohomology 1)
  (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (M.toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))

/-- Every component of `M.numericalType` maps to `closedPoint R`. -/
theorem base_numericalType_component (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    M.toBase i.1 = closedPoint R :=
  M.toBase.base_specialFiberNumericalType_component _ _ _ _ h₀ h₁ hconn i

/-- For any generator `π` of the maximal ideal of `R`, the multiplicity of a component in
`M.numericalType` is `M.toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.1`. -/
theorem coe_numericalType_multiplicity {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π})
    (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      M.toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i.1 :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_eq_of_span_eq
    ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.maximalIdeal_eq.symm.trans hπ)
    (mul_right_injective₀ (IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible R).choose_spec.ne_zero) i.1

/-- The weight of a component in `M.numericalType` is `dim_k H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_numericalType_weight (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    ((M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).weight i : ℕ) =
      M.toBase.specialFiberWeight (M.base_numericalType_component h₀ h₁ hconn i) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The intersection matrix of `M.numericalType` is the special-fibre intersection matrix of
`M.toBase`. -/
@[simp]
theorem numericalType_intersection (i j : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).intersection i j =
      M.toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix M.toBase.coheight_le_succ_of_relativeDimensionLE
        (M.toBase.base_genericPoint_ne_closedPoint (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field R)) i j :=
  (rfl)

/-- The genus of a component in `M.numericalType` is `dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` over its constant
field `κᵢ = Γ(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`. -/
@[simp]
theorem numericalType_genus (i : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).genus i =
      Module.finrank
        Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
        (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
          (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(i.1 : M.total)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Two components of `M.numericalType` are adjacent if and only if they are distinct and their
closures in `M.total` meet. -/
theorem numericalType_adj_iff (i j : (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Component) :
    (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).Adj i j ↔
      i ≠ j ∧ (closure {(i.1 : M.total)} ∩ closure {(j.1 : M.total)}).Nonempty :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_adj_iff _ _ _ _ h₀ h₁ hconn i j

/-- For any generator `π` of the maximal ideal of the discrete valuation ring `R`, and any proofs
of the codimension bound and generic-point separation, `M.numericalType` is equal to
`M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType`. -/
theorem numericalType_eq_specialFiberNumericalType
    (hX : ∀ x : M.total, coheight x ≤ 2)
    (hη : M.toBase (genericPoint M.total) ≠ closedPoint R)
    {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π) :
    M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn =
      M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη hπ hreg h₀ h₁ hconn :=
  M.toBase.specialFiberNumericalType_congr _ _ _ _ h₀ h₁ hconn hπ hreg

/-- Every component of `M.numericalType` has multiplicity one if and only if the scheme-theoretic
special fibre of `M` is reduced. -/
theorem forall_numericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff :
    (∀ i, (M.numericalType h₀ h₁ hconn).multiplicity i = 1) ↔
      IsReduced (specialFiber R M.toBase).left :=
  M.toBase.forall_specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity_eq_one_iff _ _ _ _ h₀ h₁ hconn

end ModelAPI

end TauCeti.Model

end
